menu "sys_remote"

    config SYS_REMOTE_WATCH_MS
        int "Remote read period (ms)"
        default 100
        range 10 60000
        help
          A remote device that is not wired is read from a watch's copy: the
          first read makes an ON_CHANGE watch on its board, which reads every
          this long and sends at least every twice this long.

    #@limit @alias Remote subscriptions
    config SYS_REMOTE_SUBSCRIPTIONS
        int "Subscriptions to this board's devices"
        default 16
        range 1 64
        help
          Peers subscribed to a device of this board (SUBSCRIBE): each gets the
          device's events and errors. Another board's remote device takes one.

    config SYS_REMOTE_ALIASES
        int "Remote devices with events"
        default 16
        range 1 64
        help
          Remote devices of this board whose events and errors come here: the
          board, the id there and the count of the frames that came.

    config SYS_REMOTE_QUEUE_SIZE
        int "Queue (bytes)"
        default 1024
        range 256 8192
        help
          The events and errors on their way: out to the subscribers of this
          board's devices, and in from the boards of the remote devices. A
          multiple of 4.

    config SYS_REMOTE_TASK_PRIO
        int "Task priority"
        default 4
        range 1 20

    config SYS_REMOTE_TASK_STACK
        int "Task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384

endmenu
